{"mappings": [{"technique_id": "T1053.002", "technique_name": "Scheduled Task/Job: At", "tactic": "Execution", "confidence": 0.85, "rationale": "The ATSvc RPC interface (UUID 1ff70682-0a51-30e8-076d-740be8cee98b) is the legacy 'at' service. OpNum 0 (JobAdd) and OpNum 1 (JobDel) called remotely show someone creating or managing At jobs to run code on another host, which is a common lateral movement pattern."}, {"technique_id": "T1053.005", "technique_name": "Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task", "tactic": "Execution", "confidence": 0.5, "rationale": "On modern Windows, jobs submitted through ATSvc are registered and run by the Task Scheduler service. The activity may therefore show up as, or be categorized as, remote scheduled task creation (e.g., Impacket atexec)."}, {"technique_id": "T1053.002", "technique_name": "Scheduled Task/Job: At", "tactic": "Persistence", "confidence": 0.3, "rationale": "Remotely created At jobs can also be scheduled to recur, which would give the attacker persistence on the target host beyond one-time execution."}]}
